{"source":"function Unresolved_b6b55f25(uint256 arg0) public view {
        if (0x04 + (msg.data.length - 0x04) - 0x04 >= 0x20) {
            require(uint8(uint256(store_f) / 0x010000000000000000000000000000000000000000) == 0, CustomError_9e87fac8());
            require(arg0 >= uint256(store_c.length), CustomError_3261c792());
        }
        revert();
    }","notes":"The probe calls deposit(100) and expects ok=true. The original body ends in an unconditional revert(), so every call reverted (candidate step 0 ok=false). The reference succeeds, so the success path must return instead of reverting. The guard block (paused check via store_f byte 20, min-deposit check arg0 >= store_c.length) is kept as-is since the reference passes the same checks with paused=0 and min=1 (store_c.length==1 after setLimits(1,100000)); only the terminal revert is replaced by a return. The deposit bookkeeping itself (balance/totalSupply updates seen in steps 1-3: balance 0x44b = 1000+100, totalSupply 0x44b, stats) is handled by the paired writer/getter units, not this view-guard; this unit only needs to validate and return successfully, matching observation step 0 (ok=true, no revert data, no logs)."}
